# Cloudflare Pages security headers for the HTML site (nihon101.com).
# The API (api.nihon101.com) sets its own deny-all CSP in the Worker; this governs
# the rendered pages, where the real XSS surface is (user-authored post bodies —
# sanitized at write, with this CSP as the second layer).
#
# NOTE on script-src 'unsafe-inline': Astro emits a few per-request inline scripts
# (define:vars, is:inline) and inline <style> from define:vars, and a static
# _headers file can't carry a per-response nonce. So inline is allowed, but every
# EXTERNAL origin is still locked down (no third-party script/frame/connect can be
# injected). To drop 'unsafe-inline' later, move to Astro's nonce-based CSP.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https://api.nihon101.com https://i.ytimg.com https://*.ytimg.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.nihon101.com; frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self' https://accounts.google.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), browsing-topics=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
